\begin{didyouknow}{The Most Precise Measurement}
Frequency is the quantity physicists measure best. Modern optical atomic clocks reach fractional uncertainties around $10^{-18}$, which corresponds to drifting less than a second over the age of the universe. Yet even they obey the basic rule of this section: to resolve two frequencies separated by $\Delta f$, you must observe for a time of order $1/\Delta f$.
\end{didyouknow}
