\begin{didyouknow}{Prony's 1795 Fit}
In 1795 Gaspard de Prony published a method for fitting data with a sum of exponentials by turning the problem into polynomial root finding. With complex exponents those exponentials become oscillations, so Prony's method extracts frequencies and damping rates from short data records. Variants are still used in power systems and signal processing more than two centuries later.
\end{didyouknow}
